  'mamelodi-football-court-reopens-up-campus-2026-11-07',
  'Refurbished football court reopens at UP''s Mamelodi campus',
  'Community', '2026-11-07', 'Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/local-news/2026/11/07/state-of-the-art-sports-facility-opens-in-mamelodi/',
  'A R1.35 million revamp has reopened a children''s football court at the University of Pretoria''s Mamelodi campus for players from under-11 to under-19.',
  'A children''s soccer pitch on the Mamelodi campus of the University of Pretoria has reopened following a R1.35 million upgrade that laid down new artificial turf shipped in from the Netherlands and put up stronger fencing around the playing area. Originally laid in 2010 under the city''s FIFA World Cup legacy programme, the pitch has become a base for structured after-school soccer coaching for youngsters aged from under-11 up to under-19. Local development body Rhiza Babuyile led the project. It teamed up with football charity the Johan Cruyff Foundation, while the Netherlands'' diplomatic mission in Pretoria also backed the work.

University officials said the upgraded facility gives young people in Mamelodi a safe space to build football skills while also opening doors to other opportunities. The campus''s acting director, Dr Edwin Smith, said not every player at the court would go on to a professional career, but the facility could still help them reach university study and other paths. Rhiza Babuyile''s Netherlands-based director, Robbert Popken, said the Johan Cruyff Foundation''s courts give young people in communities an alternative to gangs and violence, describing the sites as more than just places to play sport. A local coach at the court, Petrus Malobola, said having the revamped facility in Mamelodi means a great deal to the community and should help draw more promising young players to the campus.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/local-news/2026/11/07/state-of-the-art-sports-facility-opens-in-mamelodi/", "https://www.timeslive.co.za/news/south-africa/2026-10-27-university-refurbishes-mamelodi-football-court-in-r135m-project/"]',
  'agent'
);
